sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Acknowledgment, provider readback, and partial recovery
    accDescr: The applying host reads current managed labels, adds a required label when needed, and reads the provider state again before removing an obsolete managed label. An ambiguous response leads to observation rather than blind retry. Earlier verified work remains real when a later operation fails; the result is partial, not rolled back.

    participant Host as Applying host
    participant GitHub as GitHub provider

    Host->>GitHub: Read current managed labels
    GitHub-->>Host: Observed current state

    alt Required label is already present
        Host->>Host: Record a verified no-op
    else Required label must be added
        Host->>GitHub: Add required managed label
        alt Response is clear
            GitHub-->>Host: Request acknowledged
        else Timeout or ambiguous response
            GitHub--xHost: Outcome remains unknown
        end

        Host->>GitHub: Read labels before retry or removal
        GitHub-->>Host: Current observed labels

        alt Required addition is observed
            Host->>GitHub: Remove obsolete managed label
            alt Removal readback matches
                GitHub-->>Host: Intended managed state verified
            else Later operation fails or source moves
                GitHub-->>Host: Earlier addition remains verified
                Host->>Host: Return partial or incomplete application
            end
        else Required addition is not observed
            Host->>Host: Stop and do not remove or claim success
        end
    end
